UNIT U ack  # a short acknowledgement with nothing to answer: a nod, maybe a light new topic
VOCAB fair  # a word a detector reads: known, so never read as a typo of another word
VOCAB true  # a word a detector reads: known, so never read as a typo of another word
VOCAB bet  # a word a detector reads: known, so never read as a typo of another word
VOCAB cool  # a word a detector reads: known, so never read as a typo of another word
VOCAB nice  # a word a detector reads: known, so never read as a typo of another word
VOCAB word  # a word a detector reads: known, so never read as a typo of another word
VOCAB gotcha  # a word a detector reads: known, so never read as a typo of another word
VOCAB interesting  # a word a detector reads: known, so never read as a typo of another word
VOCAB same  # a word a detector reads: known, so never read as a typo of another word
UNIT D ack.0  # detector for '^ okay|alright|fair|true|bet|cool|nice|word|gotcha|interesting|facts|same $' (a short acknowledgement with nothing to answer: a nod, maybe a light new topic)
TAP ack.0 0 0 pos:end 1  # '^ okay|alright|fair|true|bet|cool|nice|word|gotcha|interesting|facts|same $': needs pos:end at 0..0
TAP ack.0 0 0 pos:start 1  # '^ okay|alright|fair|true|bet|cool|nice|word|gotcha|interesting|facts|same $': needs pos:start at 0..0
TAP ack.0 0 0 w:okay|w:alright|w:fair|w:true|w:bet|w:cool|w:nice|w:word|w:gotcha|w:interesting|w:facts|w:same 1  # '^ okay|alright|fair|true|bet|cool|nice|word|gotcha|interesting|facts|same $': needs w:okay|w:alright|w:fair|w:true|w:bet|w:cool|w:nice|w:word|w:gotcha|w:interesting|w:facts|w:same at 0..0
BIAS D ack.0 -2  # AND of the 3 required parts of '^ okay|alright|fair|true|bet|cool|nice|word|gotcha|interesting|facts|same $'
LINK U ack D:ack.0 1  # '^ okay|alright|fair|true|bet|cool|nice|word|gotcha|interesting|facts|same $' is one way of saying: a short acknowledgement with nothing to answer: a nod, maybe a light new topic
UNIT D ack.0.1  # detector for '^ okay|alright|fair|true|bet|cool|nice|word|gotcha|interesting|facts|same @laugh $' (a short acknowledgement with nothing to answer: a nod, maybe a light new topic)
